        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "qvFX8",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1114,
          "name": "cap",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "WHAT MOVED",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hvu7d",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1136,
          "name": "notes",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "THE OVERLOAD — the pane header today carries six things: icon, name, CHAT chip, status dot, “idle”, Stop, ⋯. In a 3-pane split that is three 34 px bars repeating what the header title already says.\n\nTHE LINE — 26 px: icon · name · status dot · ⋯ on the left cluster, and × alone at the far right. Both glyphs are always present ($text-low at rest, $text-mid on hover). No chip (the icon already says chat vs terminal), no status word (the dot says it), no Stop button on the bar.\n\nWHY ⋯ AND × SIT APART — a menu glyph and a close glyph adjacent in the same corner is a mis-click waiting to happen, and the two are not equally forgiving: ⋯ opens something you can dismiss, × takes a pane out of the split. Putting ⋯ against the name and leaving the flex spacer between them means the destructive one owns its corner alone, which is where every other app trains you to expect it.\n\nONE PANE, NO LINE — a node with a single pane shows no identity line at all, which is what the app already does (`grouped` gates the pane header, surfaces/panes.rs:1212). The line appears exactly when a split makes identity ambiguous, which is also when there is room to spare.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "REpOg",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1136,
          "name": "notes",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "THE ⋯ MENU — Stop (⌘.) · Rename… · Archive chat. Close pane is NOT in it: the × is always visible at the opposite end, so duplicating it would only pad the menu.\n\n× IS A LAYOUT ACTION, ARCHIVE IS A SESSION ACTION — this is the whole rule. × removes the pane from the split and the split re-flows; the chat's session is untouched and stays in the sidebar, reopenable. Archive ends the session and leaves the pane in place, empty. Acting on the layout changes the geometry and spares the session; acting on the session spares the geometry.\n\nTERMINALS COLLAPSE THE TWO — a shell has no conversation to preserve, so × kills the process and drops the pane, and Archive does not apply to it at all. Confirm before killing only when a foreground process is still running; a shell at its prompt closes silently.\n\nAN EMPTY PANE KEEPS A STUB LINE — dashed icon, “Empty”, and a × (no ⋯: there is no session to act on). Without it the Archive path dead-ends in a pane no mouse could remove.\n\nDOWN TO ONE PANE — closing 3 → 2 → 1 makes the last pane lose its identity line, because a single-pane node has none. Coherent, and it keeps “the line exists to disambiguate” true at every step.\n\nSTILL OPEN — whether a terminal pane carries a dot once its process exits, or falls straight through to the “Shell exited” card.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
