        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ykVTz",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 540,
          "name": "cap_decisions",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "DECISIONS",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jFilI",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 562,
          "name": "decisions",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "OWNED BY THE MISSION, NOT A TAB — one drawer per mission, docked under the center column (Feed or runner tab), beside the rail rather than under it. Switching Feed ↔ runner tabs swaps the surface above; the drawer and its active shell stay put. Per-runner drawers and a drawer inside the rail were rejected: a build or test watcher belongs to the mission's tree, not to whichever slot is selected.\n\nNOT A SLOT, NOT A PARTICIPANT — a drawer shell is a \"shell\" direct session started at the mission cwd; it never gets a mission_id or slot_id, never posts to the Feed, never shows in runner statuses, the rail, attention, or the sidebar. Mission routing, Runner messages, and events cannot see it. Stop / Resume act on slots only.\n\nTOGGLE — the one existing toggle-terminal-drawer action (⌥F12 default) dispatches by surface: a chat tab toggles its tab drawer, a primary non-archived mission toggles its mission drawer. No second keymap entry. The header glyph sits before the rail glyph; the tooltip reads the effective binding.\n\nENTRY POINTS — ⌥F12, the header glyph, and the palette's New terminal (when a primary mission is active) open the drawer and add a shell. Sidebar New terminal stays a terminal-only tab. cwd: mission cwd → project directory → default working dir → $HOME.\n\nABSENT ON — archived missions and secondary duplicate workspaces. The primary workspace owns shell interaction and the persisted state; a second window on the same mission shows no toggle and no drawer.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "UFZP1",
          "x": 760,
          "y": 562,
          "name": "decisions_2",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 640,
          "content": "HIDE IS NOT CLOSE — chevron, ⌥F12, the header glyph, and ⌘W from a focused drawer terminal all hide; shells keep running. A chip's × kills that shell with the foreground-process confirmation; closing the active chip selects its left neighbour; closing the last chip hides the drawer.\n\nLIFECYCLE — archiving or deleting the mission closes every drawer shell and drops the persisted drawer state. Closing a runner tab never touches the drawer. Leaving the mission for a chat, another mission, or Settings keeps shells running and restores open state, height, chip order, and the active chip on return.\n\nPERSISTENCE — 280 px default, clamped 120–600, dragged by the hairline; a drag released outside the handle still commits. A serde-defaulted { open, height, shells, active } object on the mission node's layout (the same wire shape as a tab's drawer). An older mission row reads as hidden, 280 px, no shells. Any reconciler that wraps uncovered direct sessions into tabs treats ids in a mission drawer as covered.\n\nRELAUNCH — mission drawer shells come back through the same launch-claim path as tab drawer shells (fresh shell at the recorded cwd, no replay). This does not widen the direct-shell recovery policy after an abrupt exit — tracked separately.\n\nONE MODEL — the drawer type (clamp, chip selection, hide-on-empty) is lifted out of PaneLayout and shared with the mission layout; the strip is one element both surfaces call. Two copies of the chip rules is a defect.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE — a drawer per runner or inside the rail; a shell that follows the selected runner; promoting a shell to a crew slot; splits, reorder, rename, profiles; moving shells between a mission and a chat tab; an interactive secondary workspace.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PTaM8",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 190,
          "name": "cap_header",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "HEADER — SAME TWO CLUSTERS: THE LEFT ACTS ON THE MISSION, THE RIGHT TOGGLES A SURFACE. NO FORK, NO SPLIT; THE RAIL GLYPH ONLY SHOWS WHILE THE RAIL IS CLOSED",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
